Estellus-MW is an SME located in Coueron (France). It has been recently created and it originates from Estellus (Paris, France), created in 2009. Estellus-MW is an engineering company specialised in the processing and exploitation of microwave satellite data for earth observations. The services developed by the company are based on the expertise of their employees, who are international experts in their fields.
Estellus-MW provides services in the following areas:
&bull; The development of radiative transfer modeling algorithms and inversion methods for the processing of satellite microwave observations;
&bull; The production of geophysical data from satellite observations, particularly those obtained from microwave instruments;
&bull; The creation, evaluation, and interpretation of time series of geophysical products derived from satellite observations, for environmental and climate studies;
&bull; The contribution to the design of new earth observation instruments in the field of microwave radiometry;
&bull; The preparation of microwave instrument simulators in order to assess the performance of newspace missions and prepare for the exploitation of their data.

The ITA is a public, non-profit research technological center attached to the Department of Presidency, Economy, and Justice of the Government of Aragon. Its mission is to contribute to the technological development of companies and increase their competitiveness.
ITA carries out R&D&I projects, providing multidisciplinary technological knowledge through a team of more than 280 highly qualified technologists. This team's scientific and technical excellence is oriented toward solving your business needs in a personalized way, with the aim of making your company more competitive and excellent through innovation and technological development.
The core values of support, collaboration (linkage), and technology transfer reinforce the partnership with companies in R&D&I projects. Companies consider us as their own innovation and R&D teams, relying on us to provide cutting-edge technologies aimed at adding value in the design of new products, the improvement and optimization of processes, and support in the creation of new disruptive business models.
ITA has defined five strategic areas of action to respond to the challenges of society, always offering their technological know-how:
Safe, sustainable, and connected mobility;
A digital agribusiness that responds to the demand for healthier and safer food;
An efficient industry that is fully digitized and focused on the circular economy;
Smart health that improves people&rsquo;s lives;
Clean energy that favors efficiency and the use of renewable energies.
These areas are interconnected due to global societal demands, and by addressing them together, ITA aims to create a more digital, green, and social world.
